		{
			dependencies: ["6A7BE998C2EC882D"]
			description: [
				"Right-clicking the key can &9&lset the output port of the GT machine &rand &9&lto connect the tube &r, while right-clicking the mouse can &9&lrotate the machine &rand &9&llock the flow pipe &r(the off-hand cannot have items at this time), or it can be used in its place as a pickaxe to destroy the machine."
				""
				"The screwdriver can use &9&lto open the machine cover plate configuration interface &rand &9&lto set whether the automatic output is on."
				""
				"Cable cutters can connect cables &9&l"
				""
				"The right soft hammer key can &9&lto quickly pause the &rmachine, and the right sneak key can &9&lto pause the &rmachine after the end of this recipe cycle (to resume, you can only right-click and not sneak)."
				""
				"A crowbar can &9&lremove the cover plate"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"wrench:"
				"When you hold a wrench and point it at a block where it can be used, a grid of nine squares will be displayed on each side of the block:"
				"Among them, the center is the largest, the edges are the second, and the corners are the smallest."
				"By right-clicking on the center of the machine face, you can rotate the front to that face (non-GT machines with face distinction only) or adjust the output port to that face (for GT machines); by right-clicking an edge, you can rotate face to face with the direction of the corresponding edge; When you right-click a corner, you can rotate the face to the opposite side of the right-clicked face. But if the right-click is a non-GT machine without facial recognition, the above operations will disassemble the machine. By right-clicking the center of a face, you can rotate the front face to that face (for all machines), and the others are the same for edges and corners. For non-GT machines without surface distinction, the machine must be disassembled for the above operations."
				"When you right-click the center of a pipe face, there is no change; however, right-clicking an edge can connect/disconnect the pipe in the direction of the corresponding edge; Right-clicking the corner can connect/disconnect the tube in the opposite direction. Shift-right clicking can control whether the corresponding surface should be inserted."
				"You can turn by right-clicking on logs, hay blocks, comparators, repeaters, pumpkins, jack-o'-lanterns, pistons, sticky pistons, launchers, launchers, furnaces, chests, trapped chests, ender chests, and hoppers that are not in front of you;"
				"It can be dismantled by right-clicking in front of a workbench, bookshelf, pumpkin, jack-o'-lantern, piston, sticky piston, launcher, launcher, furnace, chest, trapped chest, ender chest, or hopper."
				"But in addition to these, blocks such as levers and rails can still be rotated or dismantled."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Soft hammer:"
				"Right click to turn on/off the machine."
				"Right-clicking a lit redstone lamp can turn it off and vice versa."
				"Right click on the power rail to activate it directly and vice versa."
				"Right-click on a log, hay block, piston, sticky piston, launcher, launcher, pumpkin, pumpkin, furnace, chest, trapped chest, or hopper to rotate the block;"
				""
				"screwdriver:"
				"Used to adjust various output ports and synthetic parts."
				"By right-clicking on the front of the machine and on the output port, you can adjust whether input to the output surface is allowed."
				"Note: Although holding a screwdriver against wires and tubes does indeed produce a grid of nine squares, the actual measurement has no effect."
				"Correct statement: If the surface corresponding to the nine-square grid can be controlled by a screwdriver, this is equivalent to directly controlling the surface; if not, it has no effect. And the operating rules are the same as a wrench."
				"By right clicking on the comparator or repeater you can rotate."
				""
				"Crowbar:"
				"Used to pry rails and open various boxes, as well as remove cover panels."
			]
